        "#### 1. the Pairwise association rules by calculating confidence\n",
        "- conf[(a, b)] = pair_counts[(a, b)] / item_counts[a]\\\n",
        " =  confidence of the rule a → b\n",
        "- calculates *how often b appears when a appears*, and stores the result in conf.\\\n",
        "pair_counts[(a, b)] — get the number of times a and b appear together.\\\n",
        "Store the result in conf, using the tuple (a, b) as the dictionary key.\n",
        "\n",
        "- create Association rules from pair_counts and item_counts\n",
        "- results (eg) :\\\n",
        "conf(blue fish => red fish) = 0.818\\\n",
        "conf(one fish => red fish) = 0.809\\\n",
        "conf(two fish => red fish) = 0.797\n",
        "\n"
      ],
